@startuml
title Jenkins Test Flow For T11

start

:Jenkins server starts job;
:Jenkins assigns build to agent or executor machine;
:Agent checks out repo into workspace;
note right
Example workspace:
/home/mniedziolka/jenkins-agent/workspace/at_1
end note

:Jenkins runs bash_helper.sh from the checked out repo;
:bash_helper.sh resolves its own directory;
note right
SCRIPT_DIR is derived from BASH_SOURCE[0]
end note

:bash_helper.sh runs T11/tests/run_test.sh;
:run_test.sh prepares environment;
note right
WORKSPACE_DIR
ALLURE_RESULTS_DIR
PYTHON_BIN
end note

:run_test.sh sources T11/tests/.env.sh;
:run_test.sh runs pytest with -k div or mul;
:pytest discovers tests and loads tests/conftest.py;
:remote_calc_command fixture reads SSH env vars;
note right
CALC_SSH_PASSWORD
CALC_SSH_USER
CALC_SSH_HOST
CALC_REMOTE_PATH
end note

:test file calls execute_command with operator args;
:tests/helpers.py runs subprocess.run(...);
note right
The fixture builds the SSH command.
The helper executes it.
end note

:sshpass and ssh connect to remote machine;
:Remote machine runs calculator binary;
:stdout result returns to pytest;
:test asserts expected result and Allure stores report data;

stop

@enduml